# Complement of a pointy polyhedron, projected on i

M 1

# projection along j
2 3
  1 0 0
  0 0 1

D 1

# a pointy polyhedron: i=0 then i>=2
4 4
  1  1  0 0
  1 -1  0 10
  1 -1  3 0  # j >= i/3
  1  1 -2 0  # j <= i/2

# LBLComplement
F 16

# the complement of this pointy LBL should be:
- all j's, with i outside of [0, 10]
- plus one point i=1, because
the shadow of the LBL is {i=0} U {2 <= i <= 10}
(there is no integer j for i = 1 (1/3 -> 1/2))
